### Dana mints a service token for her billing integration: it acts in Acme as a dispatcher, and may only read jobs.
### The secret is in this answer and in no later one.
# @name DanaMintsBilling
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [201]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/auth/v1/tokens
Authorization: Bearer {{DanaAccess}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "billing",
  "kind": "service",
  "tenantId": "{{AcmeId}}",
  "roles": ["dispatcher"],
  "scopes": ["work_orders:read"],
  "expiresAt": "{{BillingExpiresAt}}"
}

### Billing reads Acme's completed jobs. A token carries its tenant, so it sends no X-Alvo-Tenant.
# @name BillingReadsCompleted
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?status=eq.completed&order=reference.asc
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{DanaMintsBilling.response.body.$.token}}

### And tries to write one: a dispatcher may create jobs, a `work_orders:read` token may not
# @name BillingTriesToWrite
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [403]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{DanaMintsBilling.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenant_id": "{{AcmeId}}",
  "reference": "{{OtherJobReference}}8",
  "title": "Billing writes a job",
  "status": "new",
  "priority": 5,
  "access_code": "ACME-BILLING",
  "customer_id": "{{AcmeCustomerId}}",
  "region_id": "{{RegionId}}"
}

### Theo mints a personal token for his phone's widget: it acts as him, in Acme, read-only. It carries no roles of its
### own — it holds his tenant roles, read on every request.
# @name TheoMintsPersonal
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [201]
POST {{fsBaseUrl}}/auth/v1/tokens
Authorization: Bearer {{TheoAccess}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "phone widget",
  "kind": "personal",
  "tenantId": "{{AcmeId}}",
  "scopes": ["work_orders:read"],
  "expiresAt": "{{TheoTokenExpiresAt}}"
}

### His token reads what he reads: his job, and only his
# @name TheosTokenReads
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/api/work_orders?order=reference.asc
X-Alvo-Api-Key: {{TheoMintsPersonal.response.body.$.token}}

### The tokens Dana minted, as she sees them
# @name DanaListsTokens
## TEST-EXPECT-STATUS: [200]
GET {{fsBaseUrl}}/auth/v1/tokens
Authorization: Bearer {{DanaAccess}}
